# README table of contents

Every `README.md` (any path, any case) must have a **Contents** section near the top: after the H1 and any short intro, before the first real section.

When you create, edit, or restructure a README, **update the Contents list in the same change**. Add, remove, rename, or re-nest links so they match the current headings. Never leave a stale TOC.

- Link every `##`, `###`, and `####` heading (skip the H1 and the Contents heading itself).
- Nest list items to match heading depth.
- Use GitHub-style slugs: lowercase, punctuation stripped, spaces to hyphens.
- Do not invent sections that are not in the file.

```markdown
# Docker stacks

Short intro.

## Contents

- [Commands](#commands)
- [How the Meteor image is built](#how-the-meteor-image-is-built)
  - [Multi-stage Dockerfile](#multi-stage-dockerfile)
- [Mongo data and volumes](#mongo-data-and-volumes)

## Commands
```
